\\frac{292}{0.73} \\approx 400\n  \\]\n\n## Conclusion:\nThe total number of students who appeared for the exam is approximately 400. \n\n\\boxed{B}", "clean": "## Reasoning:\n\n- 25% अभ्यर्थी गणित में अनुत्तीर्ण हुए: 25/100 * x = 0.25x\n- 12% अंग्रेजी में अनुत्तीर्ण हुए: 12/100 * x = 0.12x\n- 10% दोनों विषयों में अनुत्तीर्ण हुए: 10/100 * x = 0.10x\n- दोनों विषयों में पास (उत्तीर्ण) हुए: 292 अभ्यर्थी\n\n## Key Concept:\n- The total number of students can be found by adding the number of students who failed in each subject and then subtracting the number of students who failed in both subjects (to avoid double counting).\n\n## Calculation:\n- Total failed in either subject = 0.25x + 0.12x - 0.10x = 0.27x\n- Total passed in both subjects = 292\n- Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion, the total number of students is:\n  \\[\n  0.27x + 292 = x\n  \\]\n  Solving for x:\n  \\[\n  0.27x + 292 = x \\implies 292 = x - 0.27x \\implies 292 = 0.73x \\implies x = \\frac{292}{0.73} \\approx 400\n  \\]\n\n## Conclusion:\nThe total number of students who appeared for the exam is approximately 400. \n\n\\boxed{B}"}]}}
